<title>USA: Santee Cooper sees S.C. coal unit back late Weds.</title>
<headline>Santee Cooper sees S.C. coal unit back late Weds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Carolina-owned utility, Santee Cooper said Wednesday its 270 megawatt coal unit in Moncks Corner, S.C., shut early Wednesday, will likely return to service tonight.</p>
<p>&quot;We had a breaker malfunction. The unit should be back on-line by about 8 p.m. (2000 EST) tonight,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The unit is located about 30 miles north of Charleston, S.C.</p>
<p>Santee Cooper serves 103,893 electricity customers.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
